Track ambient model els on Structure

Structure grows `pub ambient_model_els: BTreeSet<ElId>`. walk_rule
inserts the enclosing-model elements it seeds there. These are the
only elements that have no recorded term in semantic_el and, by
construction, never legitimately land in a type conflict class.

emit_type_conflict simplifies: it picks one term in semantic_el
whose class is the conflict class and emits a single
CompileError::ConflictingTermType at that term's location. If no
such term exists the function panics, distinguishing ambient from
non-ambient classes in the message to help diagnose the invariant
violation. No fallback Location(0, 0) anymore.
